<title>USA: Life Re to buy AML Acquisition Co.</title>
<headline>Life Re to buy AML Acquisition Co.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Life Re Corp said Wednesday it agreed to buy 79 percent of the common stock of privately-held AML Acquisition Co for about $12.6 million.</p>
<p>A Life Re spokesman said he expected the company to close the deal in the middle of the third quarter. He added Life Re had not yet determined the manner of payment.</p>
<p>AML's founder, Dix Druce, will remain with the company and keep a 21 percent stake, a Life Re statement said.</p>
<p>AML, a Jacksonville, Fla.-based holding company, owns American Merchants Life Insurance Co.</p>
